hello see zis world and welcome to the  first episode of a new webseries called  true fear in this webseries I'm going to  be stepping outside the world of fiction  to talk about some real-life scary  stories that have happened in the world  and I know that they're true because  they personally happened to me  this episode will detail my late-night  run-in with a creepy urban sleepwalker  or at least that's what I thought was  going on  here's how it went down so it started  when I was on my way home from my  girlfriend at the Times house she was  going to visit family that weekend so I  went up one last time to visit her  before she left so basically I ended up  walking home pretty late at night and  also this is not the best neighborhood  I've heard gunshots  apparently there's a meth issue so I'm  crossing over the last intersection to  get back to my apartment and there's  just this guy standing there at the  corner this guy had dark skin he was  wearing a dress shirt he had a tie on  he had a messenger bag over his shoulder  who's wearing black pants and he was  just a pretty tall and intimidating  figure I'm waiting for the light and I'm  standing perpendicular to where he's  standing the light changes and he  doesn't move I'm getting kind of nervous  because I have to cross over this way  and basically cross in front of him to  get back to my apartment so all this  stuff is going through my head I'm  thinking is this guy gonna mug me is he  mentally ill is he insane it looks like  he's just standing there waiting for me  so I crossed the street as I get closer  to him I feel like he's gonna say  something to me and I try not to make  eye contact but I just started to get  this feeling that he's gonna reach out  and grab me or something as I cross in  front of him I steal a glance and I  noticed that his eyes are just closed so  I'm walking back to my apartment and I'm  thinking what's going on with that guy  that's pretty creepy that he's just  standing there with his eyes closed and  the idea that he was sleepwalking hadn't  really come to me I honestly just  thought he was kind of a weirdo at this  point as I get to my apartment I'm just  thinking more and more about how weird  that whole situation was I want to go  and get some video evidence of it but I  kind of doubt that the guy's still  standing out there after quite a few  minutes so I grabbed my roommate who's  also into mysterious things tell him  about the situation and we go to check  it out sure enough the guy has not moved  whatsoever so we get out there we're  behind him now about 50 feet away and  it's just quiet it's 2:00 in the morning  there's no people out there's no cars  out and we're keeping our voices down  low  we talked about him so that he doesn't  hear us if he is awake as we're debating  whether or not to get closer I snap a  quick photo and video now it's pretty  far away it's not the best evidence and  it's at night so it's a little bit hard  to see but the figure is just really  creepy standing there at the end of the  corner and it's the only evidence that I  have from that night  so finally we decide ok we'll just walk  forward we'll walk past him see what  happens check things out and as we get  closer the guy just drops and he catches  himself with his left leg and he's  almost like in the stretching position  like he's lunging to the left and he  gets to that position we just freeze  we're like ok what's going on here then  he proceeds to stick in that position  for quite a while longer we're not  exactly sure what to do and I know I  probably should have gotten another  picture at this part but I honestly felt  like this guy was going to turn around  at any point so finally we're waiting  around for a little bit he doesn't do  anything and we decide to get closer  again and as we're walking up to him he  stands up looks around seems kind of  confused and then just starts walking  forward across the street and disappears  into the night we don't bother following  him because at this point we figured  that whatever was going on with him he'd  snapped out of it he'd woken up so this  is when we came to the consensus that  maybe he was sleepwalking maybe he was  just walking home from his second job or  something he was really tired got to the  stoplight closed his eyes and fell  asleep standing up for a few minutes or  maybe he was sleeping in his apartment  and started sleepwalking all the way out  to the street and just stopped there  though that doesn't really explain the  attire he was wearing I contacted my old  roommate recently to see if he had any  recollections about the night and he  suggested that it may have been drugs  and looking back on it I think that's  kind of a theory that makes sense  leave your theory in the comments though  but what's really scary to me is to  think about what could have been for  example what if this guy had stopped  walking a few feet forward and just  stopped in the middle of the street or  what if he really was mentally ill and  dangerous and I just happened to walk by  while his eyes were closed or what if he  was sleepwalking and he would have woken  up right while I was going by and  freaked out who knows would have  happened to me so I was really  interested in this and for a few nights  after that I went outside around the  same time to go check and see if he was  there to see if this was like a common  habit that maybe he's sleepwalking at  the same time every night but I never  saw him out there again I did however  see other things which were perhaps more  scary which I'll talk about in the next  episode of true fear so subscribe if you  have not already also special shout out  to my buddy West Dakota for helping me  film this video go check out his channel  he does day  vlogs but like don't just not check it  out actually go check it out right here  get out here  if you liked this video remember to like  this video and I'll see you in the next  one  assuming we both survived
 

